WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.960
Mr. Maou...

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:14.010
Chi... I have to go back to Ente Isla.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:19.680
Oh, no... I don't want you to!
I don't want us to be separated!

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:24.020
I'm sorry. But I can't stay in this world any longer.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.150
Then I'll go to Ente Isla, too!
Please take me with you!

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.150
That, I can't do.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.160
By rights, you and I live in different worlds.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.160
We should never have met.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:43.160
Chi. I'm sorry.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.420
Mr. Maou...

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.090
Mr. Maou!

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.980
And that was my dream! The end.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.610
A dream where I go back to Ente Isla, eh?
So, what happens to me next?

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.410
Huh? After that?

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.700
Well, you...

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:25.210
Well, whatever. I can't go now anyway.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.420
I don't have enough magic left.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.250
Man, yesterday was exhausting!

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.970
After the fight I had to restore all the broken buildings...

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.640
Not to mention open a Gate and toss Sariel through it.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.190
I used up all my magic!

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.650
I see...

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.570
Hey Chi, where's Maa?

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:51.730
Here!

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.690
Kawa-cchi told me.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.530
You grabbed a mop and ran out last night, and you never came back?

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.280
Ah, well, you see...

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.580
There were some circumstances...

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.250
Why are you making excuses too?

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.750
The good Sadao saved us last night.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.920
Good evening.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.880
Looks like Crestia Bel's visiting Maou's restaurant.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:20.260
Your voyeurism is in very poor taste, even if it is for surveillance pur--

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.970
So you didn't stop at Emilia-- you planted a tracker on Bel, too!

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.310
How much did it cost?!

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.560
Hey, don't touch me with soapy hands.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:31.060
Excuse me, but...

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.190
My name is Suzuno Kamazuki.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.110
Good Chiho and I were attacked by a deviant last night on our way home,

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.570
and the good Sadao rushed to our aid.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:46.040
Y-Yes, he did! I don't know what would've happened to us if not for him!

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.870
You fought him off with a mop?

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.750
Y-Yes, he was a bit of a tough customer...

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.800
Well, I suppose that counts as extenuating circumstances.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.630
Excuse me! Miss Kisaki, a man came out of the refrigerator!

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.300
--Who <i>is</i> this guy?
--Sariel?!

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.140
--Beats me. He does seem to be alive, but...
--I thought you ejected him through the Gate?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:08.730
--Good Sadao, perhaps the bamboo ornaments responded to the Devil's magic

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.520
--Better call an ambulance, I guess.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.810
--You <i>guess</i>?

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.730
--Yeah, I don't want to stir up too much trouble...

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.480
by opening the Gate's exit inside the restaurant?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.820
Oh, he's awake.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.190
You okay? Not dead or anything?

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.490
Beautiful.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.360
Huh?

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:24.780
How strange is fortune! In another world,
I have met the goddess of beauty!

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:30.210
O goddess, so desperate am I for thy forbidden love that I may fall from Heaven!

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.210
Who is this idiot?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.000
Actually, he's from the
Sentucky across the street...

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:42.050
My beloved! You from MgR's and I from
SFC, two irreconcilable organizations,

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.510
are the very Romeo and Juliet of the fast-food industry!

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.940
Did that fall damage your brain?
I really should call an ambulance.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:57.320
Oh, such kind words!
You are concerned for my health.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:04.740
But no miracle of medicine can cure this lovesick heart!

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:10.040
So you'd rather I call the <i>police</i>!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.370
This is what tempts angels to fall!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.960
Oh, what sweet agony!

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.640
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:38.650
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.700
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:48.410
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:59.210
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:03.720
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:10.890
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:16.690
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:21.280
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.650
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.200
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:31.580
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:39.500
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:59.610
Again, my name is Yusa, and I thank you for allowing me to assist you today.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.160
What's going on?

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.080
What is this?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.330
I rule over Hatagaya at last!
Now for my next conquest--Greenland!

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:21.920
Say what?

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.680
What a messed-up dream...

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:35.890
Well, I doubt MgR's will ever be the new Devil's Castle,

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.600
but I still can't let my guard down.

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.230
Emi, you seem kinda fired up today.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.820
I-I guess so.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.950
So, want to go get dinner together?

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.110
Sorry, I can't today.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.490
You're going to go check on Mr. Maou again?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.200
Not "check on" so much as "keep tabs on"...

00:06:55.410 --> 00:07:01.420
Seriously? Don't you think it's time you two let go of hard feelings?

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.670
Not possible.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.380
I mean, it's just complicated, you know?

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.840
"Sasazuka Station"

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.560
My village... my <i>father</i> was killed.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.600
There's no way I could ever forgive that.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:23.110
Or would--? No, anyway,
I'm a hero and he's the Devil!

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.030
And there's no telling when he might turn enemy again, like in my dream.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.950
I'm coming in!

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.530
What are you doing?

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.870
Miss Yusa!

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.790
Miss Suzuno, what are you doing?!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:40.210
Well, I made an attempt at French cooking,

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.790
so I'm feeding him Udon
Confit with Sauce Américaine.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.090
What the heck is that?!

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.050
I already said I'd be making dinner today!

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.760
And Mr. Maou, why are you just going along with it?!

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.340
Huh? But...

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.970
Miss Suzuno, aren't you his enemy in the first place?!

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:57.430
You're hand-feeding him like <i>I</i> want to!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.680
Sasaki Chiho, you're letting your true feelings show.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:02.060
You stay out of this, Mr. Urushihara.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:05.980
Mr. Maou, whose dinner are you going to eat? Mine, or Miss Suzuno's?!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.690
Ummmm...

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:12.740
Budget-wise, it'd help if you took turns bringing dinner every day...

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:14.620
Oh, it's no big deal.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.240
Th-That's right, no big deal!

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.620
<i>This</i> is the Devil?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.120
Sire.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.830
Y-Yo, Ashiya! Where have you been?!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.540
I have grave business to discuss.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.840
Wh-Why the formality?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.380
I humbly request some leave time, Sire.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.140
What? Alciel visiting his home?

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:41.020
I really don't think he's returned to Ente Isla...

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:45.480
But Alciel himself said he wanted leave.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.570
There are lots of types of vacations, though!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:52.150
Maybe he's sick of that cramped little Devil's Castle?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.950
That definitely wasn't the vibe I was getting, though.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.530
"Leave time"? What's up?

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:02.290
I'm afraid I can't speak of it here.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.710
Okay.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.920
Sorry, could you three go home for today?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.920
It sounds like Ashiya needs to talk to me.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.670
--All right.
--Okay...

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.140
Ah, yes, that <i>does</i> seem suspicious.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.600
Miss Emerada didn't know either?

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:24.100
No, although to be safe,
I'm having her sniff around

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.850
for anything suspicious happening in Ente Isla.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.490
We got caught in the rain.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:48.330
Do you think Mr. Maou might really go back to Ente Isla now?

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:52.420
I'm afraid that dream might come true...

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.220
What did you dream about?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.300
W-Well...

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.970
Come to think of it, I just had an ominous dream too...

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:01.760
What? You too?

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.310
But don't worry.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:08.810
I'll never let anything sad happen to you while I'm around, Chiho.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:20.240
So many boxes... Did they go shopping?

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.620
No, they can't have that kind of money.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.540
Could that mean...?

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.710
I got a package from Eme, so there's precedent.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.670
Did they get something from the demon realm?!

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:39.590
There really isn't anything strange going on!

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:44.560
I did have Albert look into it,

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:48.600
but no unusual trouble's been reported!

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.060
--Oh! But there is one problem!
--What?

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:55.360
I've gained a little weight recently!

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.450
That's totally irrelevant!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.820
Hmm? Emi, is that you? What are you doing?

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.450
Oh, just thinking out loud!

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.870
What the hell is that dwarf manager thinking?

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.250
Miss Kisaki.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:16.590
I'm sorry for the short notice, but I'd like you to switch my shifts.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.630
Hmm? That's unusual.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.890
Sorry. Something's come up that I can't get out of...

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:27.270
Got it. I'll work something out.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:28.520
Thank you, Ma'am!

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.400
--Let me know when you need to be out.
--All right.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.070
Sheesh, rain <i>again</i>?

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:42.740
Mr. Maou, are you going home to Ente Isla after all?

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:46.540
That's why you're taking days off?!
Don't tell me you're never coming back--

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.460
Hold up! I don't have the magic to go home!

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:52.460
But... why, then?

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.750
I...

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:58.300
Sorry. I can't tell you.

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.170
Mr. Maou...

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.610
Should we really do this?

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:20.110
Wouldn't it be better to give him the benefit of the doubt?

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.780
I'd like to, but with the boxes and everything, he's definitely plotting something.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:27.700
Our only choice is to find out the truth.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.200
--But--
--Shh!

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.290
Now we tail him.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:54.190
A construction site?

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.110
Is he planning to build a new Devil's Castle here?

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:59.320
No, that's ridiculous.

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.780
He's just working.

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:04.030
Why?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.740
What are you up to?!

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.580
We needed money ASAP.
Gotta pay for two tracking devices.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.170
Tracking devices?!

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:18.040
Urushihara bought 'em.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:21.260
He planted 'em in your bag and Suzuno's sandals.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:23.510
Wh-What?!

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:31.520
H-Hey! Stop! This is no place to draw the sacred sword!

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:35.520
And they did help me find you guys when Sariel kidnapped you, so...

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:37.350
For crying out loud!

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:43.440
Anyway, they're gonna debit our account for those next week.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:48.320
But there's no money in it.
And MgRonald's payday is after that.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:53.500
So Ashiya said, "In that case, I must acquire a temp job that pays daily."

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.960
And that's why he asked for time off?

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:02.250
Yep. So I decided to take time off to work temp, too.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.050
The temp agency must've sent Ashiya somewhere else.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.090
If that's all it was, why'd you hide it from Chiho?

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:11.350
--Mm-hmm!
--Well, I... it's like...

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:15.520
I was worried that if I told Chi, she'd feel responsible

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:19.440
since the money's for the tracker that helped me rescue her.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.190
I'm sorry, Chi!

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:25.950
I'm just glad you're not going back to Ente Isla or anything.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:30.410
So what's with the truckload of boxes you had delivered, then?

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:34.250
Say what? That's news to me, too.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.960
Boxes?

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:42.210
Wh-What do you mean?
This stuff was here when I moved in.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:45.090
Liar! We both know it wasn't.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.840
Move over!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.180
Feather beds...

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.430
Fire extinguishers...

00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.140
Water purifiers...

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.520
And there's so many of them.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:02.610
Urushihara. What the hell is this?

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:05.650
Well, like they say, you shouldn't do stuff you don't understand.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:09.280
I did some digging online, and it's apparently called a "buy-up scam"...

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:10.990
"Buy-up scam"?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.580
It's a ploy where someone comes to your door,

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:16.870
says they'll buy your used stuff, then fast-talks <i>you</i> into buying stuff.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.790
I sold him an external hard drive, but...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.170
Then he kinda made me buy this--

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:27.300
--How much? How much did it cost?
--So close, so close, so close...

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:28.720
Um...

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.760
128 thousand yen!

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:37.350
It seems you fell victim to a very underhanded salesman.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.940
Stupid sucker. Just turn those guys away!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.900
But I'm socially inept...

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:46.480
Satan, lecturing Lucifer now won't accomplish anything.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:48.570
This is the company, right?

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:52.160
"Deluxe Life International Holdings"...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:54.910
What's with the meaningless company name?

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.660
Why not give them a call?

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:03.580
Hello, this is Deluxe Life International Holdings.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:06.460
How may I help you today?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.420
The other day a door-to-door salesman

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:11.590
sold us feather beds and fire extinguishers and water purifiers,

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.550
but we won't use them, so we want to return them.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:18.600
I'm terribly sorry, Sir, but we run water purifiers when we install them

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:24.770
to make sure they work, so they're essentially used, and can't be returned.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.780
We haven't used the twenty years' worth of filters that came with them.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:34.950
They come as a set with the purifiers, so we're unable to refund just the filters.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.870
And as for the fire extinguishers, once they've been installed,

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.910
for safety reasons it's illegal under the Fire Service Act

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.540
for us to take them back, even unused.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.670
What about the feather beds, then?

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:50.630
We accept returns for those as long as they're completely unused.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.010
You mean the set of seven, correct?

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.640
No, it's a set of five.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:58.100
I'm afraid our company only sells sets of seven.

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:00.680
We can't accept sets that are short any parts, so--

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.560
Just forget it!

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:05.770
They never intended to take any returns.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:07.190
What should we do?!

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.900
--Negotiate in person?
--Negotiate in person!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.610
So this is the place...

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:15.570
Coming!

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.330
Ashiya?!

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.040
Your Majesty?! And Emilia, too?!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:23.250
What brings you here?

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.710
They gave you a temp job <i>here</i>?

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.590
That explains why the voice seemed so familiar.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.760
More to the point, what are you doing?

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.840
Merely following the procedure for handling unreasonable demands for returns--

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:40.260
No, wait! Why did he buy <i>seven</i> feather beds?!

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:44.640
I told you, he was duped!
And it wasn't seven, it was five.

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.900
But that sounds like a scam!

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.730
That's what I've been <i>tellin</i>' you it was!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:53.240
Then I've been sent here to practice fraudulent business dealings,

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.070
and I've unwittingly acted as an agent of evil?!

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:00.530
As I recall, you're a demon generalissimo.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:05.040
But now that I know, I cannot remain here another second!

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.170
Quite the fuss over here.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.670
S-Sir!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.670
Is there a problem?

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.130
Are you the jerk in charge?

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:17.090
Now, that's not nice! Why don't we talk this over calmly, like adults?

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.890
Sir, I'm sure this was explained over the phone,

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.270
but it's all in the provisions of the contract.

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:27.270
Huh? What's this about "provisions"?
I didn't see any papers!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.650
I gave you your copy. I really must ask you to follow the rules.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:34.110
Excuse me? This is a scam!

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.280
All participants consented to the deal, Sir.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.610
"Consented," my butt!

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:42.660
Who'd be dumb enough to buy seven feather beds for one rundown apartment?!

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.700
A certain someone in your home.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:49.710
Y-You bastard, you're being smug because you think we're clueless!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.720
I didn't sell any defective goods, and we agreed on the contract.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:59.840
If you want to make any more false accusations,

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:02.930
I'm willing to go settle this outside.

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:06.180
We lost...

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:10.520
Perhaps the best thing to do would be to consult the police.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:12.560
You can't rely on the police for this.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:17.240
He's crooked, but there's a contract, and we have no proof it was a scam.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:19.400
So there's nothing we can do?

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:23.280
Dammit! How are we supposed to get 128,000 yen?!

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:25.700
My apologies, Sire.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:29.830
I'm partly to blame; I've been remiss in my duties as guardian.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:34.420
Guardian...? Say, how old is Urushihara?

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:35.380
Pardon?

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:38.760
Not in the other world; in Japan.

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:44.180
Oh, I think I made him eighteen in his official records.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:47.430
In that case, I can tell you a good trick.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:51.230
What? Can we get out of paying the 128,000 yen?

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.020
What is it?!

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.440
"Cooling-Off."

00:19:55.650 --> 00:20:00.700
A guardian's consent is required for a minor to sign

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.820
any contract for an amount greater than their allowance.

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:09.080
Mr. Maou, you're Mr. Urushihara's recognized guardian...

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.790
...so the Cooling-Off Rule applies.

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:44.160
Honestly! He completely took us in.

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:48.120
Yeah, that human is sneakier than a demon.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:51.040
Still, to think <i>Emilia</i> saved us...

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.960
She's used to return-happy customers.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:56.710
Gotta get that one on the demon team someday.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.500
You jest, Sire.

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:00.760
Are you ready to order?

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.930
Yep, I'll have the same as you.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:06.640
Two Katsu Doons over here, please!

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:23.820
<i>The fingertips plucking</i> <i>the strings are like the waning moon</i>

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:30.450
<i>A faint light illuminates the world</i> <i>beyond these dying days</i>

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:37.080
<i>The music echoes coldly,</i> <i>and the sound left behind</i>

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:42.840
<i>Is permeated through and</i> <i>through with more night</i>

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:47.050
<i>The path to the moon, the faint scent,</i>

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.680
<i>The hazy edges of my vision</i>

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:53.640
<i>I messed up because you said it was simple</i>

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:56.190
<i>Was I crying?</i>

00:21:56.400 --> 00:22:03.530
<i>The sky I longed for isn't</i> <i>quite the color I pictured</i>

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:09.320
<i>If I've let my hands fall from my ears,</i>
<i>I'll just keep reaching with them</i>

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:16.370
<i>It seems I'm formed out of</i> <i>everything that slips from my grasp</i>

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:23.510
<i>The only one, all alone</i>

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:02.210
Are you stupid?

00:23:03.550 --> 00:23:05.170
Emi.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:09.130
The Devil, waiting out a red light in the pouring rain with no umbrella?

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:11.260
Shut up.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:13.060
Here.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:15.890
I tossed the umbrella I borrowed from you before, right?

00:23:16.100 --> 00:23:19.600
I'm replacing it with a new one, so take it and be grateful.

00:23:19.810 --> 00:23:20.400
Huh?

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:23.020
--Just take it!
--Uh, right.

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:27.530
Hmph.

00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:38.040
Um... thanks.

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:42.330
You're welcome.
